welcome to my tutorial on how to make an  origami butterfly in this video I will  show you how to make the butterfly using  a regular sheet of printer paper if you  have origami paper that will work fine  also what we need to do is we need to  make the printer paper into a square so  we take this corner and we fold it down  on to this side until this edge here is  aligned with this edge make a crease and  you can cut off the excess paper now  that we have a piece of square paper  that has a diagonal fold in it going  this way we want to take this corner and  fold it down to this corner and try to  be as neat as possible so now if you  open up the paper you should have an X  in it now what we do is we take the  paper and we fold it in half going this  way by taking this edge and aligning it  with this edge and you make a crease so  now if you open it you should have an X  and a horizontal line once again fold it  on the horizontal line make sure it's  nice and flat now what we want to do is  we want to lift up this first layer here  and we want to tuck this corner in  towards the center of the model where my  thumb is lift up the first layer and you  tuck the corner in just like that  and then you fold and make good creases  do the same for the left side so lift up  the first sheet tuck the corner in and  then you make the creases again  so now you should have a model that  looks just like this and this is known  as the water bomb base or the paper  balloon base now that we have the proper  base to make the butterfly you should  notice that there are two top flaps and  two bottom flaps what we're going to do  is we're going to take both of the top  flaps and as you'll notice it has a  point here we want to put this point on  the top of the triangle and when we're  doing that this edge will align with  this outer edge of the triangle also so  point it to the top and then we can make  a crease so you should have something  that looks like this and we're going to  do the same with the other top flat and  make another crease so you should have  something that looks just like this now  we're going to flip the model over and  we're going to take the bottom of the  triangle and fold it towards the top but  we're not going to fold it all the way  up to the point we're going to leave a  little bit of overhang about the width  of your thumb so take the bottom fold it  towards the top just like that and leave  about a thumb width of overhang once you  have it around there then we're going to  crease the bottom of the model all the  way across so you should have something  that looks just like this now we're  going to flip the model over again and  now you should see that here are the  tips of the flaps which we previously  folded up towards the top now we're  going to bring them down just by pulling  on them like that when you do that  you'll see that it won't go down  because it is being held by this edge  here so what you have to do is just fold  it down and this edge should start to go  towards the center of the model when it  does just push down on it and then make  a good crease to flatten it out  and do the same with the left side bring  it down and just flatten out that hood  there just like that then we're going to  flip the model over again and this time  we're going to make the head so this is  going to be the head what we want to do  is we want to fold it all the way down  as far as it can go which is basically  on this edge here fold it down and make  a crease then we're going to fold it up  just a little bit so that there's a  little bit of overhang on the other side  so fold it up just about like that and  as you'll see there's a little bit  overhang on the other side so you should  have something that looks just like this  okay so we're pretty much done with the  butterfly we just have to fold the wings  and to do that what we're going to do is  we're going to take both halves of the  butterfly and fold them down away from  us so you want to fold the butterfly in  half this way and we're just going to  make a crease along this edge here okay  now what we want to do is if you'll see  there is an imaginary line from here to  here let me draw a line just so you  could see what I'm talking about  right along there where it leaves from  the bottom of the body here up to the  edge of the where the head was and what  you want to do is you want to fold  upwards along that line so fold the  wings upwards on that line and do the  same for the other side and then just  make creases along the base here on  these edges and then all you have to do  is you just want to fold you want to  fold these wings so that the edge of it  when you're folding it down is pretty  much in line with the top of the body so  if you look at it sideways it should  kind of be lined up with the body kind  of fold it straight down like that and  just make a crease along the wings and  then just pull on it a little bit and  there you go you are done with your  origami butterfly I hope you all enjoyed  my tutorial for making the origami  butterfly I'm also thinking of making a  tutorial for how to make an origami gift  box so if you've seen my tutorial for  how to make a paper ninja star where I  show you how to interlock the flaps of a  box and also how to interlock the flaps  of the ninja star that might come in  handy that way you can give someone a  personalized gift handmade by yourself  so thank you very much for watching and  don't forget to comment rate and  subscribe to my videos
 

